{"id": "707203a6-f927-453e-a333-a4b8e7e3de8e", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This error code points to CERT_E_EXPIRED, meaning a certificate fails validation against the current system clock or timestamp. Since this server was restored from an old image, the most likely cause is a clock that's drifted too far from real time, though expired root certificates or an outdated servicing stack could also be contributing factors.

I should also flag that Windows Server 2012 R2 is out of mainstream support and now only receives updates through ESU, which may have implications depending on the current date. Before giving advice, it's worth actually checking the instance's clock and state directly via EC2 and SSM, and verifying the ESU timeline claim rather than assuming.

"}]}

